  "asr_text": "I review school budgets for the local government. I lay out the costs of managing devices and the papers on learning support on my desk, and mark them with sticky notes. Is it right to count the cost of putting phones away as spending to help students do better in school? I start to write a note about the budget review, then stop. How can I explain the link between not using phones and being able to learn? The budget can't make money appear out of nowhere. I worry that spending money on the bags could mean cutting support for students who need help with learning. At the same time, I still can't tell whether this cost is necessary. Since I decide how the money is divided, I can't avoid explaining why.",
